				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				37
			],
			"Message": "style(Cocoon): Apply consistent code formatting across entire module\n\nThis commit applies automatic code formatting across the entire Cocoon extension host module, ensuring consistent style throughout the codebase. Changes include:\n\n- Converted single quotes to double quotes for string literals across all TypeScript files\n- Reorganized and sorted import statements (grouping by category: external, internal, types)\n- Split long function parameter lists into multiple lines for improved readability\n- Standardized spacing around operators and within object literals\n- Formatted multi-line console.log and telemetry statements consistently\n\nThe affected files span the complete Cocoon module including:\n- Effect services (Bootstrap, Extension, Health, ModuleInterceptor, MountainClient, RPCServer, Telemetry)\n- Service implementations (APIFactory, Command, Configuration, EchoActionClient, ExtensionContext, ExtensionHost, FileSystem, Terminal, Window, Workspace)\n- Webview panel system (Factory, Message, Panel, Serializer, State, TypeConverter)\n- Generated Vine protocol definitions\n\nNo functional changes - this is purely a code style refactoring to improve maintainability and ensure consistent formatting across the codebase.",
			"SHA": "c2c79976c1cf24c94bd8bdf27137126358338d41"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-04T12:22:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				31
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Standardize TODO comment prefixes and improve documentation clarity\n\nThis commit refactors TODO comments throughout the Cocoon module to use consistent, descriptive prefixes that clarify the nature and priority of pending tasks.\n\nChanges include:\n- Renamed generic `TODO:` to specific prefixes: `FUTURE:` (planned enhancements), `DEPENDENCY:` (blocked by Mountain backend), `SECURITY:`, `PERFORMANCE:`, `TESTING:`, `DOCUMENTATION:`, and `LOGGING:`\n- Added references to VS Code patterns with `ARCHITECTURE-PATTERN:` and `VSCODE-LIFT:` prefixes\n- Clarified many TODO descriptions to provide more context about implementation requirements\n\nAffected files span the core Cocoon services (APIFactory, Extension, Workspace, Logger), platform abstraction layer (Environment, OS, Process), IPC protocol layer, webview panel module, and module interception system.\n\nThis documentation cleanup helps developers quickly identify: which tasks are blocked by other Elements (especially Mountain), which are performance/security concerns, and which are general future enhancements. No functional code changes.",
			"SHA": "27904e8199016d07d43f7b48fa5978df507a6634"
		},
		{
			"Author": "dependabot[bot]",
